  "title": "From Coarse Evidence to Fine Ray Samples",
  "introduction": "For one ray $\\mathbf r(t)=\\mathbf o+t\\mathbf d$, take coarse depths $t_A<t_B<t_C$ and far endpoint $t_F$, so $\\delta_A=t_B-t_A$, $\\delta_B=t_C-t_B$, and $\\delta_C=t_F-t_C$. Coarse densities determine weights and a piecewise-constant PDF; illustrative draws $f_1,f_2$ then join the coarse depths for fine evaluation.",
