    {
      "title": "Turn coarse predictions into an interval PDF",
      "explanation": "The coarse field with parameters $\\Theta_c$ queries all three positions. Its full radiance-field evaluation also uses $\\mathbf d$ for view-dependent color, but each displayed density $\\sigma_i$ depends only on position. The densities, explicit interval lengths, and preceding transmittance give $w_i=T_i(1-e^{-\\sigma_i\\delta_i})$. Normalizing these weights yields the piecewise-constant PDF $\\widehat w_i=w_i/\\sum_jw_j$ over the three displayed intervals; coarse RGB values do not determine it.",
      "sourceIds": [
        "section-3",
        "section-5"
      ],
      "claimIds": [
        "c2",
        "c7"
      ],
