      "title": "Draw additional depths from the PDF",
      "explanation": "The bounded intervals, coarse densities, weights, and normalized PDF remain available while inverse-transform sampling adds $f_1$ and $f_2$. In this illustrative placement, $t_A<f_1<t_B<f_2<t_C<t_F$. The PDF is defined across intervals, so the draws are guided by expected rendered contribution rather than by point depths alone, RGB color, or selection of only the largest density.",
