    {
      "title": "Composite the fine rendering",
      "explanation": "The sorted fine colors and densities are composited front to back using weights of the form $T_i(1-e^{-\\sigma_i\\delta_i})$, producing $\\widehat C_f(\\mathbf r)$. Ordering matters because each transmittance depends on preceding densities. The coarse interval PDF determined where extra queries were placed, while the final color comes from fine-field density and direction-conditioned color outputs.",
